From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sr-0w <Sr-0w@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 19:55:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: q6afe-dai: make DISPLAY_PORT_RX a playback widget

DISPLAY_PORT_RX is a receive port, so audio flows into it from a front end
and out to the display. Every other receive port in this file is declared
with SND_SOC_DAPM_AIF_IN, and only the transmit ports use
SND_SOC_DAPM_AIF_OUT:

  SND_SOC_DAPM_AIF_IN("HDMI_RX", ...)
  SND_SOC_DAPM_AIF_IN("SLIMBUS_0_RX", ...)
  SND_SOC_DAPM_AIF_IN("QUAT_MI2S_RX", ...)
  SND_SOC_DAPM_AIF_OUT("SLIMBUS_0_TX", ...)

DISPLAY_PORT_RX is declared as an output, so the graph runs the wrong way
around it and a playback path from a front-end mixer never powers the port.
Starting a stream then leaves the AFE port un-started and the DSP does not
answer, which surfaces as

  qcom-q6afe: AFE enable for port 0x6020 failed -110

Declare it as an input like every other receive port. While here, pass NULL
for the stream name rather than the string "NULL", matching the neighbouring
receive ports.

Signed-off-by: Sr-0w <Sr-0w@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe-dai.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe-dai.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe-dai.c
@@ -958,7 +958,7 @@
 						0, SND_SOC_NOPM, 0, 0),
 	SND_SOC_DAPM_AIF_OUT("QUIN_TDM_TX_7", NULL,
 						0, SND_SOC_NOPM, 0, 0),
-	SND_SOC_DAPM_AIF_OUT("DISPLAY_PORT_RX", "NULL", 0, SND_SOC_NOPM, 0, 0),
+	SND_SOC_DAPM_AIF_IN("DISPLAY_PORT_RX", NULL, 0, SND_SOC_NOPM, 0, 0),
 
 	SND_SOC_DAPM_AIF_IN("WSA_CODEC_DMA_RX_0", "NULL",
 		0, SND_SOC_NOPM, 0, 0),
--
2.50.1
